  "summary": "A Provo resident urged the Provo City Council on Jan. 13 to terminate the city's contract with Flock Safety, citing Fourth Amendment privacy concerns. The article gathers reactions from a BYU security official and a student, and notes the council has yet to decide on the contract's future.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "I am here tonight to urge the council to terminate the city's contract with Flock Safety",
      "paragraph_idx": 3
    },
    {
      "quote": "Multiple cities, including Santa Cruz, California; Flagstaff, Arizona; Springfield, Missouri; and Cambridge, Massachusetts, are terminating their contracts with Flock Safety.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "There is a natural tension between security and privacy",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "It is unknown what course of action the Provo City Council will take regarding its contract.",
